ENFORCEMENT RULES OF THE PROMOTION OF TRADITIONAL MARTIAL ARTS ACT

Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of these Rules is to prescribe matters delegated by the Promotion of Traditional Martial Arts Act and matters necessary for the enforcement thereof.

Article 2 (Criteria for Designation of Traditional Martial Arts Eligible for Fostering) The criteria for designating traditional martial arts eligible for fostering under Article 6 (1) of the Promotion of Traditional Martial Arts Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") shall be as follows:
1. It shall be possible to substantiate the fact of their transmission through literature, records, oral traditions, or other materials;
2. Their technical systems, weapons, dress, training systems, etiquette, and terminology shall reflect the traditional characteristics of the Republic of Korea;
3. They shall contribute to the dissemination of cultural values, including by carrying out transmission activities with facilities, personnel, and programs;
4. They shall have an established technical system and training system;
5. They shall have value as a sport, including the enhancement of physical fitness and the cultivation of character.

Article 3 (Procedures for Designation of Traditional Martial Arts Eligible for Fostering)
(1) Where the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism intends to designate traditional martial arts eligible for fostering, the Minister shall publicly announce the following matters on the website of the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism no later than 30 days before the commencement date for receiving designation applications:
1. Detailed evaluation criteria;
2. Methods of evaluation and verification;
3. The application period and method of application.
(2) Where necessary for designating traditional martial arts eligible for fostering, the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism may hear the opinions of experts.

Article 4 (Revocation of Designation of Traditional Martial Arts Eligible for Fostering, etc.) Where the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism intends to revoke or withdraw the designation of traditional martial arts eligible for fostering under Article 7 of the Act, the Minister shall notify the relevant traditional martial arts institution or organization in writing of the grounds and legal basis for the intended revocation or withdrawal, and shall allow it a period of at least 10 days to submit its opinions.

Article 5 (Methods of Qualification Examinations, etc.) (1) Qualification examinations under Article 11 (1) of the Act shall be conducted by means of a written examination and a practical and oral examination.
(2) Training under Article 11 (1) of the Act shall be provided to persons who have passed the qualification examination, through practical education and on-site training.
(3) Matters necessary for the detailed implementation methods of qualification examinations and training for traditional martial arts instructors, in addition to those prescribed in paragraphs (1) and (2), shall be prescribed and publicly notified by the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism.

ADDENDUM <No. 634, May 12, 2026>
These Rules shall enter into force on May 12, 2026.
